<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel Namuncurá</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1811–1908</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel Namuncurá was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">Mapuche</a> leader who succeeded his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-calfucura">Juan Calfucurá</a> as head of the Salinas Grandes confederation on the Argentine pampas in 1873. He fought Argentine frontier forces until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julio-argentino-roca">Julio Argentino Roca</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conquest-of-the-desert">Conquest of the Desert</a> broke his power, and he surrendered in 1884. His son Ceferino Namuncurá was later beatified by the Catholic Church.</p></div>
